# MI355 gfx950 ROCm paged-attention query over-read

## Summary

On MI355/gfx950 with ROCm, `examples/basic/offline_inference/chat.py` crashed
during vLLM engine initialization while the default full-decode CUDA graph
envelope was being prepared for `meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct`.

The first local mitigation capped graph size or routed large decode captures to
Triton, but that was only a workaround. The real failure was an out-of-bounds
query load in the native ROCm paged-attention `ll4mi` MFMA4 kernel.

## Reproduction

Run on MI355/gfx950 with access to the gated Llama model:

```bash
HF_TOKEN=<token> \
HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \
PYTHONPATH=/app/vllm \
python3 examples/basic/offline_inference/chat.py
```

Before the fix, the process completed mixed prefill/decode graph capture and
then faulted as full decode graph preparation started:

```text
Capturing CUDA graphs (mixed prefill-decode, PIECEWISE): 100%
Capturing CUDA graphs (decode, FULL): 2%
Memory access fault by GPU node-2 ... Reason: Unknown.
```

## Root Cause

The synchronized debug probe patched `paged_attention_rocm` and forced
`torch.cuda.synchronize()` after each native kernel call. The failure happened
before graph capture on the eager full-decode warmup for capture size 320.

The failing call shape was:

```text
query:       (320, 32, 64), bf16, contiguous
num_kv_heads=8
GQA_RATIO=4
HEAD_SIZE=64
block_size=16
max_seq_len=1
```

In `csrc/rocm/attention.cu`,
`paged_attention_ll4mi_QKV_mfma4_kernel` loads query as `_B16x8` chunks. For
`HEAD_SIZE=64`, each head has `HEAD_SIZE / 8 == 8` chunks. The kernel computed:

```cpp
const int qhead_elemh8 = laneid / 4;
```

On a wave64 this ranges from `0` through `15`. The final guarded load checked
only that the GQA head index was valid:

```cpp
if (final_qhead_idx < GQA_RATIO) {
  Qlocal[QHLOOP - 1] =
      q_ptrh8[final_qhead_idx * HEAD_SIZE / 8 + qhead_elemh8];
}
```

For `GQA_RATIO=4`, lanes 32..63 still had a valid `final_qhead_idx`, but their
`qhead_elemh8` values were 8..15, beyond the 8 chunks in the head. On the last
query row this read exactly one row past the tensor. The GPU fault address from
the synchronized probe matched `query.data_ptr() + query.numel() *
query.element_size()`.

## Fix

Keep the native ROCm path and guard the final query chunk load:

```cpp
if (final_qhead_idx < GQA_RATIO && qhead_elemh8 < HEAD_SIZE / 8) {
  ...
}
```

The inactive lanes now zero their local query chunk, matching the existing
invalid-head behavior.

## Validation

Native synchronized probe:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=/app/vllm VLLM_ENABLE_V1_MULTIPROCESSING=0 \
HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \
HF_TOKEN=<token> \
python3 scripts/debug_issue13_rocm_capture.py \
  --max-model-len 4096 --max-cg 320 \
  --log-rocm-paged-attn --log-rocm-paged-attn-limit 8 \
  --sync-rocm-paged-attn --generate
```

Result:

```text
call=4 sync_ok
Capturing CUDA graphs (decode, FULL): 100%
[probe.generated] count=10
[probe.done]
```

Exact Buildkite smoke command:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=/app/vllm \
HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \
HF_TOKEN=<token> \
python3 examples/basic/offline_inference/chat.py
```

Result:

```text
Capturing CUDA graphs (mixed prefill-decode, PIECEWISE): 100%
Capturing CUDA graphs (decode, FULL): 100%
Generated Outputs:
...
```

The example keeps its upstream defaults. No graph cap, test skip, threshold
change, or Triton fallback is needed for this issue.
